      "status": "independently reviewed",
      "correspondence": "The selected split-place theorem invokes the complex GL sum. Its fibers use Cartan uniqueness, and its continuation uses a second application of the input to the trivial representation. The rank-two count is an independent finite specialization.",
      "review": "A second reader checked the Cartan partition, the finite Hecke sum, the unitary twist and the coefficient bound in the pinned proofs. Independent enumeration of kernels over Z/3 and Z/9 confirms the four and twelve lattices used for the shell coefficients 8 and 38."
